{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## ROOT CAUSE PROVEN (rebar-debug Phase 1) — it is NOT a fallback failure\n\nThe ticket's premise (\"rebar falls back from the primary provider to a secondary; the secondary\n401s\") does not match the evidence. **No `fallback` chain is configured anywhere in this project**\n(`rebar.toml` `[llm.model_classes]` has no `fallback` key; `runner.py:377-379` states the chain is\n\"empty for a class with no `fallback` configured, which is every deployment until an operator opts\nin\"). Nothing fell back and nothing \"failed twice\". The 401s were **primary** calls that went to\ndirect Anthropic on a project configured for Bedrock.\n\n### The mechanism (one cause explains every symptom)\n\nThe LLM layer's config table is discovered from the **ambient** root (`REBAR_ROOT`, else the git\ntoplevel of CWD) instead of from the gate's **pinned code root**:\n\n- `model_classes.load_class_slots(repo_root=None)` → `config._read_llm_file_table(None)` →\n  `config.read_reserved_section(\"llm\", None)` → `_config_sources._discover_project_config(None)` →\n  `_config_sources.repo_root(None)` = `REBAR_ROOT` else `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` of **CWD**.\n- `current_code_root()` is never consulted on that path, even though\n  `gate_source.gate_read_root` documents the opposite invariant: *\"Activate BOTH the code root\n  (file tools) and the pinned ticket-store root, so **every config rebuilt deep in the gate reads\n  each**\"* (`src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py:120-124`). `LLMConfig.from_env` honours it for\n  `repo_path` (`config.py:550-558`) but reads the table itself from the ambient root\n  (`config.py:526`).\n\nWhen ambient discovery misses the project's `rebar.toml`, `parse_class_slots({})` silently returns\nthe built-in defaults — which are **bare Anthropic ids** (`_DEFAULT_MODEL_BY_CLASS`,\n`model_classes.py:53-57`; `standard` = `VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL` = `\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"`,\n`config.py:73`) — and `_resolve_target` infers provider `anthropic`. The result is exactly the\nstring in the report: `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6`.\n\n### Runtime proof (discriminating experiment)\n\nWith an **active gate code root** pinned to the repo and CWD outside it:\n\n    cfg.repo_path      = /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-2876\n    threaded  resolve  = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6     # resolve_model_string(c, cfg.repo_path)\n    UNthreaded resolve = anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6                # resolve_model_string(c)   <-- the 401 model\n\nReproduced a second way with CWD *inside* the repo, via the other ambient input:\n\n    REBAR_ROOT=/tmp  ->  resolve_model_string(\"standard\") == \"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n\nThis also explains the otherwise-contradictory **mixed** log: `/tmp/03ef-review6.out:8` shows a\n**successful `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-...` call in the same run** as the 401s.\nThe Bedrock call came through `workflow/runners.py:129`, which *does* thread\n`resolve_model_string(req.model_ladder[0], req.repo_root)`; the 401 calls came through the sites\nthat thread nothing — `overlap/judge.py:125,170` and `plan_review/__init__.py:87`. Threading is\nthe discriminator, and nothing else in the run differs.\n\n### Sibling call sites (same construct)\n\nUn-threaded, therefore ambient-rooted: `overlap/judge.py:125`, `overlap/judge.py:170`,\n`completion.py:452`, `plan_review/__init__.py:87`, `enrich.py:82`, `epic_bug_screen.py:109`,\n`code_review/workflow_ops.py:589`, `plan_review/sizing.py:382`, plus\n`model_classes.fallback_targets_for` / `primary_endpoint_for` (both default to\n`load_class_slots()` with no root) as called from `runner.py:362,381`. Correctly threaded today:\n`workflow/runners.py:129`, `code_review/batch_runner.py:69`,\n`plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:99`.\n\n### Second, INDEPENDENT finding — the credential in this environment is genuinely invalid\n\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` **is** set here (108 chars, `sk-ant-` prefix) and is **rejected by Anthropic**:\n\n    GET https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models  ->  HTTP 401\n    {\"type\":\"authentication_error\",\"message\":\"API key is invalid.\"}\n\nSo the key is not blanked and not unresolvable — it is present and revoked/wrong. This is an\n**operator-only** fix; per the debug protocol no attempt was made to obtain or substitute one.\nNote also `should_fall_back` (`model_classes.py:367-393`) deliberately does **not** fail over on\n`CHANGE_SETTINGS` (credential) errors — \"a credential error must not be masked by shopping for a\nprovider whose key happens to work\" — so a fallback arm can never rescue a bad key by design.\n\n### Legitimacy: `defect`\n\nThe behaviour violates a cited design invariant (`gate_source.py:120-124`, quoted above) and the\n`rebar.toml` decision record that Bedrock is the project default and an ambient-Anthropic default\nis a *leak* to be closed (`rebar.toml:139-176`). Not intended behaviour."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786098197293278001,"uuid":"cd54a131-dd72-44ed-afce-4e08e01769d6"}